title: 'Registrar: relayed para requests + deprecations'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      A para with no channel to the registrar parachain can now manage itself through the relay
      chain. It calls the new `pallet-registrar-relay::relay` with a `ParaRequest` (add or remove
      lock, deregister, schedule code upgrade, set current head), which is forwarded as
      `MessageToParaV1::Relayed` under the para id of its origin. `pallet-registrar-para` runs the
      request as the new `Origin::RelayedPara`, accepted wherever `ParachainOrigin` is, and reports
      the outcome in `RelayedRequest`.

      `pallet-registrar-relay::Config` now requires a `RuntimeOrigin` convertible into the
      parachains `Origin`, and `pallet-registrar-para::Config` one built from its own `Origin`. Both
      `WeightInfo` traits gain a function: `relay` and `receive_relayed`. `MessageToPara` no longer
      implements `MaxEncodedLen`.

      The `paras_registrar` calls in `polkadot-runtime-common` get a `Deprecated` doc note naming
      their replacement.

crates:
  - name: registrar-primitives
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-para
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-relay
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-runtime-common
    bump: none
